From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:57:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: add the MT6797 A53 cluster PLLs

Let cpufreq set the clock of the two Cortex-A53 clusters, CPU0-3 and
CPU4-7, the way the vendor kernel does:

- the PLL moves through the MCU frequency-hopping controller, which slews
  it to the new PCW while the cluster keeps running from it;
- the cluster divider grows before the PLL moves and shrinks after;
- a post-divider change runs the cluster from MAINPLL for the 2 us the
  PLL takes, opening that path in TOPCKGEN CLK_MISC_CFG_0.

For each rate the driver picks the smallest total division that puts the
VCO between 1050 and 2028 MHz, with up to /2 in the post-divider. That
gives the vendor VCO and dividers for every point of its MT6797 tables.

The secure firmware writes the A72 fields of the same mux and divider
registers, so every access holds DVFSP hardware semaphore 3, through the
DVFSP handoff that owns the CSPM window. MCU FHCTL reads can return zero
once after a write, so words are read twice, zero results repeated and
writes read back. Any failed step marks the device faulted; it then
refuses further changes.

The driver does not set the cluster voltage. It never sets a cluster
above the rate it found at probe, and refuses a post-divider change on a
cluster that started below MAINPLL, so no step runs a cluster faster
than the firmware did. It refuses to probe if a cluster is not on its
ARMPLL, its dividers are unknown, FHCTL is already hopping, or the
MCUCFG sync DCM divider, which the vendor keeps in step with the clock,
is on.

debugfs "registers" reads the live PLL, divider, mux and FHCTL state.
---
